  "worked_solution": "Recall that two integers are coprime if their greatest common divisor is $1.$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true, while statement II is false. Indeed, let's use the Euclidean algorithm, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}321 & = & 213\\cdot 1 & + & 108 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 213 & = & 108\\cdot 1 & + & 105 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 108 & = & 105\\cdot 1 & + & 3 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 105 & = & 3\\cdot 35 & + & 0\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe last positive remainder is $3.$ So, the greatest common divisor of $321$ and $213$ is $3:$\n\n$$\n\\text{gcd}(321,213)=3.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $\\text{gcd}(321,213)>1,$ the numbers are not coprime.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"",
